35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,It seems that flexibility in usage is the primary driver of satisfaction for the users.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,I found that the hidden costs of room unavailability are quite significant for the departments.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The data confirms my suspicion. Our technicians are spending far too much time on manual labor that should be automated.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings suggest a systemic issue. Projects based on ""appeal"" are consistently delayed, while mandatory repairs are on time.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"How enlightening. It appears our ""approved"" costs are mere suggestions, and our reserves are practically non-existent.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, if ""appeal"" projects fail, we should prioritize functional, shared improvements.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I agree. We must consider the disruption to the timetable as a real cost.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Victoria, if we prioritize functional improvements, we must ensure they reduce the manual burden on the staff.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that is a logical point. We need a plan that is realistic in its scope to avoid the usual slippage.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I wonder if we are all ignoring the fact that we cannot afford the luxury of ""appeal"" if we cannot even replace a projector.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, a project that serves many people efficiently is not a luxury; it is a necessity.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I am concerned that we often ignore the operational void created during the construction phase.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,I am less concerned with the construction phase and more with the permanent workload after the project is finished.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,We must find a balance. A project that looks good on paper but takes two years to finish is a failure.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. I shall be voting for the option that demonstrates the most fiscal honesty and operational sustainability.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
