60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B aligns with the need for shared, flexible space that users actually value.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option B is attractive, but we must consider the impact on the ground-floor hall's current use during the works.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,Option A is the only choice that addresses the operational strain. The ventilation upgrades would eliminate those manual routines.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Option A is a mandatory-style upgrade. Based on the delivery schedules, it is the most likely to be completed on time.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is a necessity, though I suspect the actual cost of the ventilation plant will exceed the estimate.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, @Mizuki, @Benjamin, it seems you are leaning toward A. However, B provides a broader benefit to the student body.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George"",""Mizuki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, while B is beneficial, the post-occupancy data suggests that shared spaces are only successful if they don't disrupt core functions.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"The staff cannot sustain the current manual workload. If we choose B or C, we are ignoring the people who keep the campus running.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, the risk of Option B slipping into a multi-year project is too high. Option A is a clear, functional requirement.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,I find the logic for Option A quite compelling. It is a matter of survival rather than aesthetics.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I see the consensus forming. While I value the user experience of a Commons, the operational risk of A is lower.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I will support Option A, provided we plan the installation to minimize the rooms out of service during the term.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I am satisfied with that. It is a reliable choice that provides long-overdue relief to our technicians.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,It is the most logical decision. It addresses a real need without the fluff that usually leads to budget and schedule overruns.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,A rare moment of total agreement. Let us hope the actual tender doesn't shock us too deeply.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
